-- Scale torture: the dimensions that break buffers and tables.
--
-- The 500-arm match is not arbitrary. It is what exposed a dangling
-- stack buffer in theory_pglcert.c3: the non-exhaustiveness diagnostic
-- rendered its counter-example into a `char[256]` LOCAL and handed the
-- address to the DiagBag, which prints it long after that frame is gone.
-- Small matches printed plausible text because the frame had not yet
-- been overwritten; 500 arms put enough traffic in between that the
-- compiler emitted raw pointer bytes and its own output stopped being
-- valid UTF-8.
mod torture_scale

